  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">This openly available taxonomic article has begun to attract light usage, with 83 views and 41 downloads recorded in Zenodo. The scholarly citation record is still quiet in OpenAlex, and there are no scite or public-mention signals in the current digest, so the article\u2019s visible footprint is currently centered on access and reuse rather than citation-based uptake.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The article documents <em>Nosophora parvipunctalis</em> Hampson, 1896, summarizing its type locality and distribution record, including the Indian record from Meghalaya and the global record from Burma (Myanmar). It is part of a broader open research and data-sharing workflow on Zenodo, with a linked dataset and multiple machine-readable relationships to related biodiversity resources, including GBIF and Plazi-derived infrastructure.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">In terms of measurable reach, the strongest signal is usage: the record has 83 views and 41 downloads. That pattern suggests readers are finding and retrieving the work, even though citation-based influence has not yet accumulated in the indexed scholarly record. The work is available through open access, which likely supports this early-stage visibility and reuse.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The surrounding metadata also indicates strong stewardship and interoperability. The article is connected to a Zenodo dataset and is exposed through repository and data-citation infrastructure, which increases the chance that the taxonomic content can be discovered and reused by both human readers and downstream systems. OpenAIRE has indexed an open instance of the record, reinforcing its accessibility.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">At present, however, the evidence base for broader impact remains limited. OpenAlex shows 0 citations, scite reports no citing context, and event data are unavailable, so there is no current sign of scholarly citation, public discussion, or media pickup in the record provided. The most reliable interpretation is that this is an accessible, well-described taxonomic contribution with early usage signals and clear integration into biodiversity data networks, while longer-term influence has yet to emerge in the available metrics.</p>",
